            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Disney Girl 54"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a \"must have\" at Thanksgiving. I've found that gently swirling in a cup of sour cream when the gelatin is almost set makes for a lovely marbled effect, and adds a wonderful taste."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TODDLERMOM2"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I got rave reviews at Thanksgiving when I brought this to my inlaws house! The only changes that I made were to use cranberry jello in place of cherry and to use WHOLE berry cranberry sauce instead of jellied. I also omitted the nuts totally to make it more kid friendly and it didn't seem to make a difference.",
            "datePublished": "2006-11-24T12:04:22.973Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this salad!! I think I have made it before, but had lost the recipe. It is very rich. I mixed the pecans in instead of putting them on top. It was very quick and easy. Thanks to Laura for submitting it.",
            "datePublished": "2000-04-29T19:42:59.627Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MELISSANI"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love this cranberry gelatin salad! I made this for my family's Thanksgiving dinner this year, and even people that usually won't touch cranberry sauce couldn't get enough. I highly recommend using the whole berry sauce in place of the jellied... the berries add a certain something special to the contrast. Also, rather than simply sprinkling the pecans on top of the salad, I mixed them in well with the rest of ingredients to get a little in each bite.. delicious! Be sure to get as much of the juice out of the pineapple as possible, you won't be disappointed with the result!",
            "datePublished": "2008-11-29T06:53:00.550Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Judy Cowan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe is FANTASTIC! I use sugar-free raspberry jello, I use the pineapple juice and boiling water combined to make 2 cups and I use whole canned cranberry sauce. I omit the nuts completely. I could eat a whole giant bowl of this by myself! My picky sons love it and my hubby and I fight over the left overs!!",
            "datePublished": "2009-10-13T09:18:52.070Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "footballmomnva"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe has been in our family for years and we've been making it for the winter holidays since the 70s. The only thing I do a little differently is to make sure the cranberry sauce melts into the hot jello and then I mix the chopped pecans in with the crushed pineapple and we also add a can of drined mandarin oranges. We also put ours in a jello ring mold, let it set overnight in the fridge, and then unmold and slice it like a bundt cake for serving. It's a great recipe and is easy to make and always turns out great! We even make it in the summer because it's just that good!",
            "datePublished": "2023-07-12T01:05:39.303Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KLPARR"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This salad was soooo good. A great addition to our meal. I did not have sugar free gelatin so I used regular Jello, still wonderful...the kids really enjoyed.",
            "datePublished": "2002-09-04T20:21:16.123Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TSANGLIN"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this dish for Thanksgiving and Christmas 2003, but I left out the pecans. Both adults and children loved it! It goes really well with turkey (or chicken) since there's a good balance of sweetness and tartness. My 2yr. old likes to eat it as dessert!",
            "datePublished": "2004-01-01T20:08:28.107Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lisa Cammarata Pruitt"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Too much cherry flavor. Next time I would use 1 pkg Jello (or 2 cans cranberry)... depending on servings needed. The pineapples and pecans were perfect. Thank you",
            "datePublished": "2005-01-05T06:42:10.357Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KindOrzo4379"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I added a topping made with an 8 oz brick of cream cheese softened with some of the drained pineapple (enough to make it spreadable on top of the jello after setting). Made it beautiful! Also mixed the chopped nuts into the jello mixture.",
            "datePublished": "2024-12-23T15:36:14.409Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Awesome. Made for a potluck while in Korea and it was the biggest hit. The local Koreans loved it as well as the Americans! I did not have pecans so used walnuts. Came out OK. In my opinion, leave out the nuts altogether.",
            "datePublished": "2005-01-09T18:32:11.810Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Valerie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had a recipe that used raspberries but wanted to this one out on the family. It was a hit! ",
            "datePublished": "2026-06-07T15:41:15.657Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "redangell51"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My mom would make this every holiday. It was my special salad. I wish she was here to make it again. My mom also added cut up green apples. Cut them into but size or smaller pieces. It's my favorite salad,",
            "datePublished": "2026-06-01T12:47:15.671Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a variation on my Mother's recipe. We use real cranberries, but I love the idea of using cranberry sauce! Add mini marshmallows to complete the dish and it is perfection!",
            "datePublished": "2026-03-09T18:08:37.942Z"
          },
          {
